## JavaScript Variables

Modern JavaScript primarily uses:

let
const

Example:

const name = "Ben";
let age = 20;

Prefer `const` when the variable does not need reassignment.

---

## JavaScript Data Types

Common types:

string
number
boolean
null
undefined
object
bigint
symbol

Arrays are objects in JavaScript.

Example:

