# Django + JavaScript

Django doesn't have to generate every part of the page.

You can combine:

Django
    ↓
HTML/CSS
    ↓
JavaScript
    ↓
Fetch API
    ↓
Django API

For example:

JavaScript:

async function loadPosts() {
    const response = await fetch("/api/posts");
    const posts = await response.json();

    console.log(posts);
}

Django:

GET /api/posts

returns:

{
    "posts": [...]
}

This creates a more interactive application.

